      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-317687",
      ":question/problem": "In a school club membership report, the counts of members by club and gender are shown in the table below.\n\n|  | Male | Female | Totals |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Robotics Club | $44$ | $46$ | $90$ |\n| Debate Club | $27$ | $33$ | $60$ |\n| Art Club | $31$ | $39$ | $70$ |\n| Environmental Club | $78$ | $42$ | $120$ |\n| Totals | $180$ | $160$ | $340$ |\n\nWhich club has a male count that is closest to $\\frac{1}{6}$ of the total number of males in the report?"
