      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-317874",
      ":question/problem": "At a farmers\u2019 market, the counts of shoppers by stall type and time of day are shown in the table below.\n\n|  | Morning | Afternoon | Totals |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Produce | $45$ | $27$ | $72$ |\n| Bakery | $56$ | $25$ | $81$ |\n| Dairy | $33$ | $46$ | $79$ |\n| Flowers | $66$ | $41$ | $107$ |\n| Totals | $200$ | $139$ | $339$ |\n\nWhich stall type has a Morning count that is closest to $\\frac{1}{4}$ of the total number of Morning shoppers?"
